Name: gsutil
URL: https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/gsutil
Version: 5.36
Revision: c1e99521cebd61bab214b67a00372051cb01fb7b
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: Apache-2.0
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: no
Shipped: no

Description:
gsutil is a Python application that allow access Google Cloud Storage from
the command line. gsutil can do a wide range of bucket and object
management tasks, including:
* Creating and deleting buckets.
* Uploading, downloading, and deleting objects.
* Listing buckets and objects.
* Moving, copying, and renaming objects.
* Editing object and bucket ACLs.

Local Modifications:
* Added README.chromium, BUILD.gn, gsutil.bat
* Added third_party/google-auth-library-python/google/__init__.py
* Removed docs, test, and samples (see update steps)

Steps to update:
git clone https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/gsutil foo
cd foo
git checkout TAG
git submodules init
git submodules update
cd ..
cp foo/* .
rm -rf third_party gslib/vendored
cp -r foo/third_party .
cp -r foo/gslib/vendored gslib
rm -rf foo
rm -rf **/docs **/samples
rm -rf **/tests **/test **/tests_async **/system_tests **/*_test.py
rm -rf **/.* gslib/commands/test.py third_party/mock third_party/funcsigs
Remove "mock" and "funcsigs" from gsutil.py
touch third_party/google-auth-library-python/google/__init__.py
git add .
